[font_size=24][b]Getting Started[/b][/font_size]

Gator Model Studio keeps modelling, UV editing, materials, rigging, animation, and export inside Godot.

[font_size=18][b]Basic model workflow[/b][/font_size]

[ol type=1]
Create a new document or import an existing mesh.
Add or select an object in Object mode.
Enter Vertex, Edge, or Face mode to edit topology.
Add material slots and assign selected faces where needed.
Mark seams and unwrap each material from the material panel or full UV Editor.
Apply modifiers before rigging or weight generation.
Build the skeleton, generate weights, and correct deformations.
Create animation clips and pose with FK, IK, and constraints.
Save the GMS document, then export the complete scene.
[/ol]

[font_size=18][b]Files[/b][/font_size]

[ul]
Save and Save As store the editable GMS document as a Godot resource.
Export Scene creates a TSCN, GLTF, GLB, or OBJ output for use in a project.
Auto Export on Save becomes available after the document has been exported once.
Save As clears the prior export association so a copied version cannot overwrite the original export accidentally.
[/ul]

[font_size=18][b]Where to look next[/b][/font_size]

[ul]
Materials and UV Tiles explains multiple materials and face assignment.
Rigging explains skeleton construction and weight painting.
Animation and IK explains clips, keys, IK targets, poles, and constraints.
Guided Voxel Remesh explains whole-object and selected-area remeshing.
[/ul]
